Section 16. That Section 8.60.200, Emergency abatement, is created as follows:
8.60.200
Emergency abatement.
If a nuisance exists on any property in the city that presents a substantial risk to
public health or safety and if the chief of police, or designee, makes a determination that
the nuisance must be abated on an emergency basis, the chief of police may authorize the
nuisance officer to immediately proceed to abate the nuisance without notice or hearing.
The determination of costs shall be subject to the provisions of Section 8.60.160 of this
chapter.
